      ":question/id": "cf9a45d8-93e4-5a5c-8ad1-796e86ba6570",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105606",
      ":question/problem": "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=\u27e8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,4v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\u27e9.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202u}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(4v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\u27e9 \\\\ {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202v}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(4v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,2v,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\u2061u & 0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ 0 & 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\u27e8|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u & -4v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ 0 & 4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e88{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}\u2061u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
