      ":question/id": "dade4255-e1e8-5d68-9c25-815855912b22",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109909",
      ":question/problem": "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=u-{e}^{v}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=\u27e8u,\\,v,\\,u-{e}^{v}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202u}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(v),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(u-{e}^{v})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,0,\\,1\u27e9 \\\\ {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202v}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(v),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(u-{e}^{v})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,1,\\,-{e}^{v}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\u27e8|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
