      ":question/id": "9f52e90e-7be3-5f9c-9e1c-12885e700253",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109912",
      ":question/problem": "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=\u27e8u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\u27e9.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202u},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202u}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202u}(v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\u27e9 \\\\ {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202v},\\,\\frac{\u2202z}{\u2202v}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(u),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202v}(v\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{\u2032}\\times {r}_{v}^{\u2032} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\operatorname{sin}\u2061v & -v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\u27e8|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v & -v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -v\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{sin}\u2061v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v\\end{aligned}|\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v+uv\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
